  "scope_id": "PINNING-20261031-001",
  "title": "Five three-place knots, and pinning makes cubic systems hard",
  "subject": "Which three-place laws can be decided on cubic systems, where every point lies on exactly three lines",
  "conclusion": "The 34 three-place knot relations fall into five classes (parity, Fibonacci, not-all-equal, x or (y != z), clause), and only not-all-equal has no preferred value, so only it cannot pin a value. A law that can pin a value, turn a pinned line into an equality and absorb spare occurrences is as hard on cubic systems as with unbounded occurrences, which makes the Fibonacci law and x or (y != z) NP-complete there.",
